           "type": "string",
           "value": "The paper presents an experimental demonstration of the simultaneous transmission of a 60-W power-over-fiber (PoF) signal and a high-speed discrete multitone (DMT) signal over a 1-km 7-core weakly coupled multicore fiber (WC-MCF). The DMT signal is transmitted at 50 GBaud and 60 GBaud, corresponding to data rates of 117 Gbit/s and 140 Gbit/s, respectively. The experimental setup includes a high-power fiber laser, an arbitrary waveform generator, and a photodetector. The results show that the bit error rate (BER) of the DMT signal is below the soft decision forward error correction (SD-FEC) threshold of 2E-2, and the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) meets the 3GPP requirement."
       },
       {
           "key": "step_1_concept_analysis",
           "type": "string",
           "value": "The paper proposes a novel method for high-speed signal light and high-power energy light co-transmission using a 1-km 7-core WC-MCF. The system integrates multiple advanced modulation formats, including DMT, to achieve high-rate and high-power co-transmission. The experimental results demonstrate the successful transmission of 50 GBaud and 60 GBaud DMT signals with a 60-W PoF signal, and the BER performance is below the SD-FEC threshold."
       },
