           "value": "The paper verifies the physical consistency of the reported metrics by measuring the transmission of the 1064 nm PoF signal over 1-3 km of single-mode fiber (SMF). The results show that the collected optical power increases linearly as the high-power fiber laser (HPFL) output power increases, indicating no obvious nonlinear effect of stimulated Raman scattering (SRS) at 1 km. The paper also measures the insertion loss of each channel induced by the fan-in and fan-out (FIFO) device and finds that it is less than 3 dB."
       },
