           "key": "step_3_strategic_critique",
           "type": "string",
           "value": "The paper demonstrates the potential of the proposed system for remote application scenarios, such as powering tens or hundreds of low-power consumption devices in the remote unit (RU). The system can provide stable electrical power to low-voltage loads in the Grid scenario, with a temporal fluctuation of the collected power less than 1% over 1 hour. The paper also highlights the importance of the proposed system for future digital grid applications, where high-speed data communication and high-power transmission are required."
       }
